  "body": "## What changed\n\nTool cutting data by work material (#2015, part of #2007):\n\n- **`Unknown` row.** Every tool's cutting data now holds an `Unknown` row (file word `unknown`; in code `CuttingRow::material == None`). It is what the tool runs when no row names the material in force, and the fallback for a row's missing stepdown/stepover. It is derived from the tool's own rpm/feed and stored only when it states something more (other numbers, or a step) - so a new tool has it, every older tool reads its own numbers as it, and plain tools are stored, saved and shown to MCP byte for byte as before. A command that moves the running numbers away from a derived row stores it first. A waterjet (recipes) and an electrode (rpm 0) get none, so a sane tool never turns insane.\n- **Stepdown and stepover per row** (mm, optional). They seed an operation's stepdown/stepover only inside an undoable command (quick-add, MCP `add_operation`, the feature recognizer, `SetWorkMaterial`, `SetStockMaterial`, retargeting a tool), never on load. Seeded kinds: pocket, adaptive, offset, slot, 3-D pocket, multi-axis rough, face (stepover; stepdown only when staged), 2-D contour (stepdown). A stepover wider than the cutter is refused by tool name.\n- **Setup stock material.** New `StockMaterial` component on a setup's stock and the undoable `SetStockMaterial` command (MCP `set_stock_material`, stock page \"Material\" group). The row is picked by the stock's material, then the document's, then `Unknown`. The tools' running rpm/feed (the posted S word) follow the document material only - a tool is shared by every setup.\n- **`.camtools`/project migration.** `PROJECT_VERSION` 62 -> 63 (the issue's \"61 to 62\" predates #1453's bump). A v62 project loads with each tool's own rpm/feed as its `Unknown` row; nothing it runs moves. `.camtools` reader accepts versions 1, 2 and 3; the writer writes 3 only when a library holds a stated `Unknown` row or a step (otherwise 1, or 2 for left-hand taps, as before). An `Unknown` row that only repeats the tool's own rpm/feed is not written, so plain tools save byte for byte as before (MCP `get_job` output unchanged for them).\n- **Tool page.** The \"Cutting data by material\" group is now a table: Material, Spindle rpm, Feed, Stepdown, Stepover (0 = not stated). The `Unknown` row is first, its material fixed, not removable.\n- **Behaviour change, inside a command only:** stating a document material the tool has no row for now runs the tool's `Unknown` row (before: the previous material's numbers stayed). An operation's milling feed still moves only for a row that names the material (#890's rule), so picking a material never overwrites hand-set op feeds.\n\nDecisions: `docs/decisions/2015-unknown-cutting-row.md` (why `Option<WorkMaterial>` and not a `WorkMaterial::Unknown` variant: `WorkMaterial::row()` indexes the handbook table).\n\nBase: upstream/main (`31f8d03d7`); no file overlap with #2029 (it does not touch `tool_cutting_rows.rs`; both touch `crates/ui/src/state.rs` in different places). Fork synced at the current upstream main for this branch.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `crates/tools/tests/unknown_row.rs` (6): selection order, step fallback, derivation once and only from the running numbers, kinds that get none, refusals (bad steps, `Unknown` twice).\n- `crates/app/tests/cutting_unknown_row.rs` (9): `a_new_tool_gets_its_unknown_row_from_its_own_numbers`, `a_v62_project_loads_its_tool_numbers_as_the_unknown_row_with_no_loss`, `a_v1_tool_library_loads_with_the_unknown_row_and_steps_write_v3`, `the_row_is_picked_by_the_stock_then_the_document_then_unknown`, `a_second_setup_stock_material_seeds_only_its_own_operations`, `steps_seed_only_in_commands_and_the_stock_material_round_trips`, `a_project_with_no_new_rows_posts_the_same_s_and_f_words` (posts, re-saves as v62, reloads, re-posts: identical S/F words), `a_stated_stepover_wider_than_the_cutter_is_refused_by_tool_name`, `mcp_sets_the_stock_material_as_one_undo_step`.\n- `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tests/stock_material.rs`: the stock page's Material group sits between Shape and Size, and a pick is one undoable `SetStockMaterial`.\n- Updated to the new law: `crates/app/tests/tool_cutting_rows.rs` (stating plastics, which has no row, now runs the tool's Unknown row), `crates/ui/src/egui_app/tool_cutting_rows.rs` unit tests (Unknown is shown, never added).\n\nGate: `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` (macOS, m5): green on 75031d5f9 (tools, app and ui suites; 6.2 min). Clippy on camcraft-tools, camcraft-app, camcraft-ui: clean (`--all-targets -D warnings`).\n\n## UI before and after\n\nThese are headless captures of the real egui controls, rendered with `egui_kittest::Harness::render` on Linux. Before is pre-feature commit `31f8d03d744e77ce707282d816e11efe0922f239`. After is reviewed head `af78aec60436e402c8e026d5bc9521552131bf5a`. The temporary harness called the shipping `cutting_rows` and `stock_page` functions; no UI was mocked. The cutting-data draft has the same Aluminium 6061 row in both captures. The after draft also states stepdown 2 mm and stepover 3 mm. The stock captures use the same seeded document.\n\nImages are stored only on the fork's images-only `pr-screenshots` branch, at commit `b8e36213fceb86370d85ace7865d5ac48ddf1c4d`. No capture harness, screenshot, golden, or review evidence was added to this PR branch.\n\n| Control | Before | After |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Cutting data | ![Cutting data before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b8e36213fceb86370d85ace7865d5ac48ddf1c4d/pr-2077/cutting-data-before.png) | ![Cutting data after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b8e36213fceb86370d85ace7865d5ac48ddf1c4d/pr-2077/cutting-data-after.png) |\n| Stock Material | ![Stock Material before](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b8e36213fceb86370d85ace7865d5ac48ddf1c4d/pr-2077/stock-material-before.png) | ![Stock Material after](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mkinney/Camcraft/b8e36213fceb86370d85ace7865d5ac48ddf1c4d/pr-2077/stock-material-after.png) |\n\nThe after table shows the fixed Unknown row, the named material row, and the step fields. The after stock page shows the Material group between Shape and Size. Both render checks passed at each revision (four captures total). This was a headless UI render, not a manual native-window session.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No manual native-window UI session. The controls were rendered headlessly as shown above. The release-lane pixel snapshot comparisons were not run and no golden PNG changed.\n- The camcraft-mcp skill row for `set_stock_material` is a follow-up (process-file change): #2076.\n- A per-setup spindle speed (the S word by stock material) is out of scope: the tool's running rpm follows the document material.\n\nChangelog: Tools keep cutting data per work material with an Unknown default row, an optional stepdown and stepover per row, and a setup stock may state its own material, which picks the row (stock, then document, then Unknown); older projects and tool libraries load unchanged (#2015)\n\nEffort: high (no escalation)\n\nBREAKING CHANGE: project files are written as version 63 (and tool libraries with a stated Unknown row or steps as version 3); older builds refuse them.\n\nFixes #2015\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX\n\n",
